======================================================
PART B – DOCKERFILE BASIC INSTRUCTIONS
======================================================

A standard application Dockerfile can contain:

FROM <base-image>
WORKDIR /app
COPY <source> <destination>
EXPOSE 8080
CMD ["<startup-command>"]

IMPORTANT INSTRUCTIONS:

FROM
----
Specifies the base image.

Example:
FROM openjdk:17-jdk-slim

WORKDIR
-------
Sets the working directory inside the image.

Example:
WORKDIR /app

COPY
----
Copies files from build context into the image.

Example:
COPY target/<application>.jar /app/<application>.jar

EXPOSE
------
Documents the port used by the application.

Example:
EXPOSE 8080

CMD
---
Specifies the default command when the container starts.

Example:
CMD ["java","-jar","/app/<application>.jar"]


