======================================================
PART N – IMPORTANT DOCKER CONCEPTS FOR EXAM
======================================================

1. IMAGE
--------
A Docker image is the packaged application/runtime template used to create
containers.

2. CONTAINER
------------
A container is a running/stopped instance created from an image.

3. DOCKERFILE
-------------
A Dockerfile contains instructions used to build an image.

4. docker build
---------------
Creates an image from the Dockerfile.

Syntax:
docker build -t <image-name> .

5. docker run
-------------
Creates and starts a container from an image.

Syntax:
docker run -p 8080:8080 <image-name>

6. PORT MAPPING
---------------
-p 8080:8080

Format:
-p HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT

7. EXPOSE
---------
EXPOSE 8080 documents the container port expected by the application.
It does not by itself publish the port to the host.

8. WORKDIR
----------
Sets the working directory inside the image/container.

9. COPY
-------
Copies application files into the image.

10. CMD
-------
Defines the default command executed when the container starts.

11. docker ps
------------
Shows currently running containers.

12. docker ps -a
---------------
Shows running and stopped containers.

13. docker logs
---------------
Shows container output/logs and is especially useful when the application
starts and then exits.

14. docker exec
---------------
Runs a command inside a running container.

15. docker stop
--------------
Stops a running container.

16. docker start
---------------
Starts a stopped container.

17. docker commit
----------------
Creates a new image from a container's current state.

18. docker tag
--------------
Gives an image a repository/tag name, commonly for Docker Hub.

19. docker push
--------------
Uploads an image to a container registry such as Docker Hub.

20. docker login
---------------
Authenticates with Docker Hub/registry.

21. docker logout
----------------
Logs out from the registry.


